# FloqR identity card (s3.1.41)

Resume: `@identity-card$` / `$floqr-card$`.

## Owner spec (Oct 13 2026, verbatim)

> "It is supposed to be like a gif... depending on the shoutout, if a display name is included, it plays the FloqMedia side of things before it then displays the '@handle', where '@handle' could be the person's Instagram or Mingl or Entered Name... that is how it is supposed to work!"

Owner follow-up (Oct 13 2026, s3.1.42, verbatim):

> "For Heist, I want to have 'Caught in a HEIST', then 'Presented by FloqMedia', then 'Powered by FloqR Social OS', then '@handle' where applicable."

## Per-template phase list (`identityPhases`, s3.1.42)

Templates may set `identityPhases` (array, ≤ 6 entries) on their config. Entries: `"brand"` (PRESENTED BY FloqMedia), `"handle"` (FROM @handle — dropped unless the handle resolves under the priority below; idle boards always drop it), or a fixed line `{kicker, value}` (cleaned to board capitals, ≤ 22 graphemes each, escaped like everything else). Missing / invalid / handle-only lists fall back to the default `["brand", "handle"]`. Still one `FLOQRFrameLoop.cycle("identity-card")`, 6s per phase — no template timer.

| Template | Phases with handle | Without handle / idle |
|---|---|---|
| Default (every template without `identityPhases`) | PRESENTED BY FloqMedia → FROM @handle | PRESENTED BY FloqMedia (steady) |
| Heist (`heistVaultNight`, `heistPoliceCar`, `heistInterrogation`, `heistVaultDollars`, alias `heistRedLux`) — `window.FLOQR_HEIST_IDENTITY_PHASES` in `shared-data.js` | CAUGHT IN A HEIST → PRESENTED BY FloqMedia → POWERED BY FloqR Social OS → FROM @handle | the first three |

Heist message window: `scheduleHeistMessageThenBrandSlide` stretches the message phase to at least one full card cycle (`phaseCount × 6s`) so every phase plays before the HEIST brand slide (Locked Up / Police Car / Snitch: 20s → 24s with a handle; Tengo muchos dólares: 15s → 18s / 24s). The brand slide itself (club logo, 8s) still fades the whole text overlay, card included — that is the venue's logo slide, not the card. Firestore template docs merge over packaged config, so `identityPhases` stays packaged unless a Master Admin writes one.

Board strings (CAUGHT IN A, PRESENTED BY, POWERED BY, FROM, HEIST, FloqMedia, FloqR Social OS) are brand chrome — not i18n keys, never translated.

## Behavior (every template with the pill)

| ShoutOut | Card |
|---|---|
| Idle / default CTA | Always visible, steady **PRESENTED BY FloqMedia** (subtle 6s pulse) |
| Live, no handle (or `attributionChoice: "none"`) | Same steady **PRESENTED BY FloqMedia** — never hidden |
| Live, handle opted in | GIF-like loop on `FLOQRFrameLoop`, 6s each: **PRESENTED BY FloqMedia** → **FROM @handle** → repeat |

Bug it replaced: `@keyframes classicIdentityShellBurst` (20s burst-away) hid the pill ~67% of the time; classic live ShoutOuts without `data.attribution` hid the card entirely; `startFloqrCardCycle` and the Heist rail ran their own `setInterval`s.

## Handle priority (single helper: `FLOQRIdentityCard.resolveHandle`)

1. `attributionChoice === "none"` → no handle (patron unticked "Include my handle").
2. `includeAttribution` truthy **or** non-empty `attribution` → `attribution`, formatted by `attributionChoice`:
   - `instagram` → `@handle`; `floqrHandle` / `username` / `mingl` → `@handle` (Mingl);
   - `displayName` / `manual` / `name` → entered name as typed (uppercased, sanitized);
   - missing choice → `@` only when the value starts with `@` or is a single handle token.
3. Legacy fallback (only Heist / text-overlay and split media pass `legacySubText`): pre-s3.1.41 payloads that carried the handle in `subText`, only when the payload has no `attribution`, no `attributionChoice`, and `includeAttribution` is not truthy; celebration phrases and the template `defaultSub` never count. Jerseys never use `subText` (it is the jersey mark).

Privacy: a value that looks like an email or phone number (≥ 7 digits of phone characters) is dropped → brand only. Capped at 22 graphemes; `FLOQRBoardFit.fitIdentity` shrinks long values instead of clipping. Escaping: `FLOQRSafeRender.escapeHtml` (local fallback escapes `& < > " ' \``). The shell span carries no `data-*` attribute (safe-render allowlist); the phase lives on the host (`data-identity-phase`).

## Modules

- `floqr-identity-card.js` → `window.FLOQRIdentityCard` (UMD, `module.exports` for tests): `resolveHandle`, `phases`, `phaseAt`, `shellHtml`, `mount(host, {data, idle, legacySubText, defaultSub, hostClass, shellClass, escape})`, `stop`. Loaded after `floqr-safe-render.js`, before `display-app.js`, on `display.html` and `display2.html`.
- `floqr-frame-loop.js` gained named cycles: `cycle(name, {count, holdMs, onAdvance})` / `stopCycle(name)`. The card uses channel `identity-card`. Templates still never start their own interval.
- `display-app.js` `mountFloqrCard(host, opts)` is the only entry: classic (`#displaySub`, `classic-bw-identity`), Heist / text-overlay (`heist-identity-rail`, `heist-identity-shell`), jersey + NFL dual (`#displayIdentityRail`, `soccer-jersey-rail floqr-card-bottom`), Christine, split media / birthday. Fallback without the module = brand only (never a patron value).
- `display.css`: `floqrIdentityCardIn` (.5s, min opacity .6) + `floqrIdentityCardPulse` (6s, opacity 1) + one-shot `floqrIdentityParticleBurst`. Per-template pill styles kept. NFL `nflFloqrCardPulse` unchanged. Burst keyframes deleted.
- Composer (`patron-app.js` `floqrCardAttributionFields`): every template stamps `includeAttribution`, `attribution`, `attributionChoice` (`"none"` when unticked); preview URL carries `attributionChoice`. Checkout + Club Admin approve already copy these fields → no Functions change.

## Decisions

- s3.1.41 retired the Heist footer lines; s3.1.42 brought them back by owner request as Heist `identityPhases` (above), on the shared loop.
- display2 idle stays the SupRstar idle screen (no card, by design).
- Full / neon templates keep their plain sub line (no pill added).
- Board strings PRESENTED BY / FROM / FloqMedia are brand chrome, not localized.
- Untouched: `classicFitStyle`, idle text fit (s3.1.40), `data-is-96x48` naming, display health diagnostics. Xibo URLs stay `display.html?location=` / `display2.html?location=`.

